The input workbooks of the tasks trace_dependents and find_index_match_cells
come from SpreadsheetBench-v2 (file data_example_05_11.zip,
https://huggingface.co/datasets/KAKA22/SpreadsheetBench-v2/blob/main/data_example_05_11.zip), licensed under the MIT License; that license, in
licenses/MIT-SpreadsheetBench-v2.txt, applies to those two workbooks.

The job postings in the three job tasks (long_bulk_categorize-job-titles,
long_bulk_extract-salary-range, long_bulk_summarize-job-descriptions) come
from the Kaggle dataset rashikrahmanpritom/data-science-job-posting-on-glassdoor
(https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rashikrahmanpritom/data-science-job-posting-on-glassdoor,
Uncleaned_DS_jobs.csv), listed as CC0. Its description says the postings were
scraped from Glassdoor, so the right to redistribute their text is not
established; they are not covered by CC BY 4.0. Recruiter names, emails and
phone numbers are replaced.

The product listings in the two product tasks (long_bulk_translate-catalog,
synth-rewrite-description-inplace) are taken from the product pages of
Decathlon's online store (names, prices, attributes and descriptions).
They are not covered by CC BY 4.0.

The app review texts in the five review tasks are rewritten from reviews on a
public Google Workspace Marketplace listing and are not covered by CC BY 4.0.

